	category: 'X++ PrimArrays'!
PrimArray comment:
'Array objects in smalltalk vary in size, while in x++ they allocate separate storage for the varying part.  Thus they require very different Recipes.

Recipes are normally registered by the class'' associated Recipe class at its own initialization time.  In smalltalk, the Array classes share a common Recipe class, (STArrayRecipe), which registers an instance of itself for each appropriate concrete subclass of PrimArray.X.

UInt1Arrays are odd in smalltalk, and get normal recipes generated by the normal smalltalk stubble mechanism

(WeakPtrArrays are not in the browser because they currently have no clients and may disappear.)'!

(PrimArray getOrMakeCxxClassDescription)
	attributes: ((Set new) add: #ON.CLIENT; add: #DEFERRED; add: #EQ; yourself)!

!PrimArray methodsFor: 'accessing'!

{void CLIENT login} at: index {Int32} storeValue: value {Heaper | NULL}
	"Store a value in a PrimArray, may be a Heaper, NULL, or a PrimValue.
	It is expected that most PrimArray clients will want to use less abstract
	access methods."
	self subclassResponsibility!

{Int32 CLIENT login} count
	"How many elements the array can hold"
	
	^self basicSize!

{Heaper | NULL} fetchValue: index {Int32}
	"Fetch a value from a PrimArray, may be a Heaper, NULL, or a PrimValue.
	Clients are expected to perform necessary casting.  It is expected that
	most PrimArray clients will want to use less abstract access methods."
	self subclassResponsibility!

{Heaper CLIENT login} getValue: index {Int32}
	"Fetch a value from a PrimArray, may be a Heaper, NULL, or a PrimValue.
	Clients are expected to perform necessary casting.  It is expected that
	most PrimArray clients will want to use less abstract access methods."
	
	
	| result {Heaper} |
	result _ self fetchValue: index.
	result == NULL ifTrue: [Heaper BLAST: #NotInTable].
	^result!

{PrimSpec CLIENT} spec
	"A description of the kinds of things which can be stored in this array"
	
	self subclassResponsibility!

{Heaper CLIENT} valueAt: index {Int32}
	"Get an individual value from the array. It may be a primitive data type, or a pointer to an object. Blasts if it is NULL."
	
	| result {Heaper} |
	Ravi knownBug. "primitive types stuff"
	result := self fetchValue: index.
	result == NULL ifTrue:
		[Heaper BLAST: #MustNotBeNull].
	^result! !

